{"user": "What are some general tips for playing Othello?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T02:32:25.716366+00:00", "assistant": "On this board, the game is already over: **no empty squares remain**.\n\nGeneral Othello tips:\n\n- **Corners are king**: once you take a corner, it can never be flipped.\n- **Avoid X-squares** early/midgame: b2, g2, b7, g7 \u2014 they often give away corners.\n- **Avoid C-squares** next to empty corners: a2, b1, g1, h2, etc., unless you\u2019ve calculated it.\n- **Mobility matters**: good moves leave your opponent with few legal moves.\n- **Don\u2019t chase big flips early**: flipping many discs can make you vulnerable.\n- **Stable discs matter**: edge/corner-connected discs that can\u2019t be flipped are valuable.\n- **Endgame = count exactly**: with few empties left, calculate final disc totals, not just position.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T02:32:25.716366+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T02:32:30.716366+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
